From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mf, mfreadwrite: audio renderer policy and clock rate, empty video capture enumeration, EVR stream GetService, class factory LockServer

Stubs, as documented now:

- The streaming audio renderer's IMFAudioPolicy (E_NOTIMPL): the grouping
  parameter, display name and icon path round-trip (defaults GUID_NULL and
  empty strings), are handed to the renderer's audio session whenever one
  exists (also after the audio client is made again), and fail with
  MF_E_SHUTDOWN after Shutdown; E_POINTER for NULL out parameters.
- IMFClockStateSink::OnClockSetRate of the audio renderer: S_OK (MF_E_SHUTDOWN
  after Shutdown); the samples are rendered at the rate the clock hands them out.
- MFEnumDeviceSources for video capture: S_OK with no devices now also
  clears the returned array pointer (it was left as the caller's garbage).
- The EVR stream sink's IMFGetService: MF_E_UNSUPPORTED_SERVICE for a service
  it does not offer, not E_NOTIMPL.
- The mf and mfreadwrite class factories' LockServer: S_OK without the FIXME.

---
diff --git a/dlls/mf/evr.c b/dlls/mf/evr.c
index eb366ea..434bdd5 100644
--- a/dlls/mf/evr.c
+++ b/dlls/mf/evr.c
@@ -673,9 +673,9 @@ static HRESULT video_stream_get_service(struct video_stream *stream, REFGUID ser
         return E_NOINTERFACE;
     }
 
-    FIXME("Unsupported service %s.\n", debugstr_guid(service));
+    WARN("Unsupported service %s.\n", debugstr_guid(service));
 
-    return E_NOTIMPL;
+    return MF_E_UNSUPPORTED_SERVICE;
 }
 
 static HRESULT WINAPI video_stream_get_service_GetService(IMFGetService *iface, REFGUID service, REFIID riid, void **obj)
diff --git a/dlls/mf/main.c b/dlls/mf/main.c
index e74a4ae..c09e70a 100644
--- a/dlls/mf/main.c
+++ b/dlls/mf/main.c
@@ -534,8 +534,9 @@ static HRESULT WINAPI class_factory_CreateInstance(IClassFactory *iface, IUnknow
 
 static HRESULT WINAPI class_factory_LockServer(IClassFactory *iface, BOOL dolock)
 {
-    FIXME("%d.\n", dolock);
+    TRACE("%d.\n", dolock);
 
+    /* the factory is static: there is nothing to keep loaded */
     return S_OK;
 }
 
@@ -762,7 +763,10 @@ HRESULT WINAPI MFEnumDeviceSources(IMFAttributes *attributes, IMFActivate ***sou
 
     if (IsEqualGUID(&source_type, &MF_DEVSOURCE_ATTRIBUTE_SOURCE_TYPE_VIDCAP_GUID))
     {
-        FIXME("Not implemented for video capture devices.\n");
+        /* no video capture device can be enumerated here, so the list is empty */
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_MF_ENUM_EMPTY
+        *sources = NULL;
+#endif
         *ret_count = 0;
         return S_OK;
     }
